From 21f87ab209f76fc4ad4f1dcdec923c66a03a5066 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:59:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): external-run card state (light blue / red),
 watch adapters, hover fields [daveey]

Cards parked on work that runs elsewhere (awaiting kind ci/deploy/external) get a derived state:
external_running / external_unknown / external_down, with `external` {service, adapter, job, health, reason, url,
observed_at, next_due_at} on wait info and kanban_external / _unknown / _down counts plus kanban_external_cards
(cap 10) on session rows (interface.md, interface-hover.md).

- kanban_external_state: pure clock-injected state machine (1 failed poll or 429 = unknown; 2 consecutive
  down/unreachable, auth_failed, host silent > 2x every, or no watch = down; terminal job wakes, a failed job is
  not an outage; 429 honours retry_after and never counts toward red).
- kanban_external_adapters: github_run / github_pr_checks (wrap kanban_ci_progress, fetch= injection kept) and
  shell (legacy rc 0/1/3/other + optional `HERMES_WATCH {json}` line).
- kanban_external_watch: records as `external_watch` task_events (the Board sync has no per-card LWW table:
  spike in the card), wake with external_result, shared blocker service-down.<adapter>.<scope> (one probe card
  woken, cleared on the first ok poll, external_recovered event).
- Wired into kanban_ci_progress.sweep and kanban_wake_check.apply_result; read side in
  kanban_external_activity (wait info overlay, session counts/cards).

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_external_{state,adapters,watch,activity}.py.
